{"request_sha256": "8bac70476dce40af59e70c6c41ef79bcfcea6d96a8192e025e1ce1814c872903", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "079e4ceac8aed04b27a48a3e8a632fedaff39ad5e82227cccf66760e5dcd7067", "schema_sha256": "30f41622e6c7560e23f9cf8ab8aee356761b3ddea7cb1a9d1835cabc34f30ac0", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 7578}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["rosette-crown-fronds (seed 1, P-WHOLE): the crown is a flat radial starburst of ~25 very short, very thin, sparse-leafleted rays; no frond arches, none droop below the crown base, and the crown spread is only ~2-3x trunk diameter against the references' broad recurved hemisphere. Defining mismatch with crown-pinnate-arching-fronds.", "rosette-crown-fronds (seed 42, P-WHOLE): same failure mode; rays are marginally longer but still straight, thin and non-drooping.", "owner-fronds-long-arching (seeds 1 and 42): the owner's first-dial requirement is unmet - leaflet size and frond length remain far below reference proportion and the lowest fronds do not droop.", "owner-trunk-straight-constant (seeds 1 and 42): the trunk is visibly wavy, with a pronounced dogleg/S-kink at roughly mid-height and a second bend below the crown, plus marked basal-to-apical taper. This is the owner's explicit 'never wavy, near-constant diameter' requirement and reads as a defining mismatch, not acceptable lean variation.", "trunk-character (seed 1, P-TRUNK): the drawn trunk surface is smooth with faint vertical striation only - no retained leaf-base stubs, no spiral/diamond lattice, no fibrous matting. Assessed as drawn; the organs are known-unlanded (fn-110) but the cell still does not match trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern or trunk-fibrous-matting.", "leaf-base-close (seed 1, P-BASE): the close view resolves the trunk surface clearly and shows the same smooth striated cylinder; the leaf-base pattern is absent rather than unresolvable. The ground/base junction is out of frame, so basal-flare is separately unknown.", "fruit-clusters-pendent: no inflorescence or fruit bunch is drawn on either seed. Owner scoped this to fn-111 for a later pass, so it is a known gap rather than a surprise, but it remains an unmatched core reference trait in this comparison."], "observations": ["Both P-WHOLE seeds show a single unbranched stem carrying one apical crown - solitary and unbranched holds; only the 'roughly constant diameter' half of solitary-columnar-stem fails.", "Both P-WHOLE seeds show a completely bare trunk: no epiphytes, no sprouts, no foliage below the crown. This satisfies owner-trunk-bare on both seeds.", "Leaflets in the render read as short dark dashes strung along thin rachides; they are neither the narrow stiff lanceolate blades nor the plumose V-section of leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow, and the black speckling suggests very small or degenerate leaf quads rather than a shading choice.", "Seed-to-seed behaviour is consistent: seed 42 differs only in slightly longer rays and a slightly shallower mid-trunk bend, so the failures are systematic rather than per-seed noise.", "The P-TRUNK render (render-3) is framed wide enough to show the crown and upper trunk and confirms the crown-shaft-absent reading (frond bases sit directly on the trunk) - the one core-adjacent trait the render happens to match.", "The spruce anchor (anchor-0) shows the expected finish floor (dense foliage mass, coherent silhouette); the palm crown is far below that density, but this is recorded as a finish observation only and no morphology weight is taken from the anchor.", "No cell was failed for lack of photorealism; every failure above is a silhouette- or structure-level mismatch with the reference-only inventory or an explicit owner priority.", "Relative to the owner's note that fronds were 'far too thin and short today', the current crown may or may not be an improvement - no prior render is in evidence here, and improvement would not change the absolute readings above."], "findings": [{"observation": "Crown is a radial starburst of short, thin, sparsely-leafleted rays with no arch and no fronds drooping below the crown base, against a broad recurved hemispherical rosette of 30-60 long plumose fronds in the references.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with frond length and leaflet scale being set far below reference proportion, as the owner already suspected; the render alone does not establish which dial is responsible."}, {"observation": "Trunk carries a pronounced mid-height dogleg and a second bend below the crown on both seeds, with clear taper from base to apex.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The host note records taper at 1.0, outside the authored 0.05-0.6 band and where the owner does not want it; a trunk-curvature source separate from taper would also produce the waviness. Neither is established by the images."}, {"observation": "Trunk surface at close range is smooth and faintly striated with no leaf-base stubs, no spiral lattice and no fibrous matting.", "evidence_ids": ["render-1", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The trunk organs (fn-110) are stated as not landed; the render is consistent with that, but is reported here as what is drawn, not as an excused absence."}, {"observation": "No pendent fruit bunches are present on either seed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Date cluster is scoped to fn-111 and explicitly not landed in this pass."}, {"observation": "Trunk is bare over its whole length on both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "A single unbranched stem carries one apical crown on both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The epiphytic ferns and vines in reference-1/reference-2 are scene features of those specimens, not species character; their absence from the render is correct and is in fact required by owner-trunk-bare.", "evidence_ids": ["reference-1", "reference-2", "render-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Foliage colour in the render is a dark green flecked with black; the references span deep green to grey-glaucous, so colour is within acceptable variation and is not counted against the candidate. The black flecking itself is a render artefact question, not a colour question.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Could be single-sided leaflet quads, sub-pixel leaflet geometry, or a normal/backface shading issue; not distinguishable from these images."}, {"observation": "No dead-frond skirt is drawn beneath the crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The trunk/ground junction is outside the frame of the P-BASE view, so basal-flare cannot be assessed from this evidence.", "evidence_ids": ["render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Crown density and silhouette coherence fall well below the fn9 spruce finish floor, though the anchor governs finish only and contributes nothing to the morphology verdicts above.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "anchor-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Core. Render crowns are flat radial starbursts of short straight rays; no outward-downward arch, no recurved older fronds, no drooping lowest fronds. References show a rounded hemisphere-to-shuttlecock crown of many long arching fronds. Defining mismatch."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Core. Leaflets read as short sparse dark dashes along a thin rachis, giving a bare ladder rather than the dense plumose V-sectioned frond with bristly spreading tips seen in all three references. Assessed as a structural mismatch, not a finish complaint."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-1", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Core. The close trunk view resolves the surface clearly and shows a smooth, faintly striated cylinder with no stubs and no spiral diamond lattice. Absent as drawn; known-unlanded (fn-110) is the likely reason but does not convert the cell to unknown, because the surface is fully visible."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-1", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Core. No reddish-brown fibre or shredded husk anywhere on the drawn trunk; the interstitial matting that fills the reference lattice has no counterpart."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Core, split result reported as fail on the balance. Single and unbranched is supported on both seeds. 'Roughly constant diameter' is not: the trunk tapers visibly from base to crown and is interrupted by a dogleg, which also breaks the owner's explicit near-constant-diameter requirement."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Core. No inflorescence stalks or fruit bunches drawn on either seed. Recorded as an unmatched core trait; the owner has scoped the date cluster to fn-111, so this is an accepted gap for this pass rather than an unexpected regression."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary. No brown collar of collapsed dead fronds below the crown. Observed in one reference only; refinement, not a blocker."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Variation. The render's dark green sits inside the deep-green to grey-glaucous span the inventory itself flags as indistinguishable between lighting and cultivar causes."}, {"trait_id": "petiole-base-orange-sheath", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. The crown apex in the render is too small and too dark to resolve petiole bases or any sheath material; neither presence nor absence is assessable."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Inventory calls this variation (strong lean and S-curve in reference-0 vs vertical in reference-1/2), and on the inventory alone the render's curve would be tolerable. The owner's authoritative priority narrows the acceptable range to straight-or-gently-leaning and never wavy, and the render's abrupt mid-trunk dogleg is outside it. Reported as fail against the owner priority, with the inventory contradiction stated rather than suppressed."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation, and scene-specific rather than species character. Render trunk is bare, which matches reference-0 and satisfies owner-trunk-bare."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-1", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary. The render's warm dark grey-brown falls within the mid grey-brown to reddish-brown range; only the lighter bleached stub faces are missing, and those depend on the unlanded stubs."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-1", "render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary. The P-BASE view is framed above the ground junction, and the whole views are too distant to resolve a root boss. Inventory itself marks this uncertain in the reference. Unassessable in both directions."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. Frond bases sit directly on the trunk with no smooth green columnar sheath between crown and trunk, matching the reference."}, {"trait_id": "basal-leaflet-spines", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary and uncertain in the inventory itself. Proximal frond detail is below resolution in every render view, so no reading is possible."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Inventory marks this variation with unmeasurable exact ratios, but the render is outside even a generous band: crown spread is roughly 2-3x trunk diameter and frond length a small fraction of trunk length, where the references show a crown several times the trunk width. Reported as fail because it is the same deficit the owner names as the first dial, not as a measurement claim."}, {"trait_id": "owner-fronds-long-arching", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Owner priority 1, both seeds. Fronds remain thin and short, leaflets tiny, and no lowest fronds droop below the crown base."}, {"trait_id": "owner-trunk-straight-constant", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Owner priority 2, both seeds. Pronounced mid-trunk dogleg plus a second bend, with visible taper."}, {"trait_id": "owner-trunk-bare", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "render-3"], "explanation": "Owner priority 3, both seeds. Nothing grows on the trunk over its full drawn length."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"2826e993-0da9-402e-a88d-9202625e512f","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","workflow-launch-exec","reload-plugins","reload-skills","rename","ultrareview","security-review","usage-credits","extra-usage","usage","insights","recap","skill-doctor","goal","design-consent","design-revoke","list-agents","team-onboarding"],"terminal_slash_commands":["doctor","color","reload-plugins"],"apiKeySou